      "identity": "JCM680 explicitly names L-Cysteine HCl H2O solution (10 mL); CHEBI:91248 denotes the one-water hydrochloride solute. The local named partial stock is supported. Current MAPPING_SEMANTICS section1 expressly allows solution→solute broadMatch; unknown concentration and absence of an is_a ancestry do not prevent that scoped relation. The inherited closeMatch is not supported by its historical no-subclass rationale. Recommend broadMatch plus the exact local registry sibling, preserving all concentration/formulation/role/export limits. No source or row change is made. This is an inherited #342/#321 predicate issue, not a new W07 source-alias defect.",
